---
/**
 * website/src/pages/caps-and-costs.astro — the caps-and-costs guide (website plan, Task
 * W1.5; reworked by the owner's brief of 2026-10-19).
 *
 * The page is a heading, the one message a reader meets above the fold, and the guide
 * itself: what a job costs, the commands that set the caps, and what the owner's own
 * aggregation publishes are `src/components/CapsCosts.astro`, which renders the owner's
 * measurement and the CLI's own reference. Nothing is written here, and nothing on this page
 * is a figure neither of those sources produced (F26, F31, F33, D96, D97).
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import CapsCosts from '../components/CapsCosts.astro'
---

<Base title="Caps and costs">
  <h1>Caps and costs</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    A cap is a ceiling on what a run may spend: <code>observe</code> counts and logs,
    <code>enforce</code> halts. What Fugaro's own jobs cost, and the commands that set the
    caps.
  </p>

  <CapsCosts />
</Base>

<style>
  /* The page's own lead, in the site's tokens (W1.2, D104): no colour is named here. The rule
     is the one `community.astro` and `faq.astro` carry for their own leads — Astro scopes a
     component's styles to its own markup, so a `class="lede"` this page writes needs the rule
     in this page's block or it renders as body text. */
  .lede {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }
</style>
